# $netBefore v1 2026-09-09 (restorenet v1) — the net for a RESTORE.
# Puts the LIVE class into pVaultRef under <cls>_before, so a restore onto the
# wrong class can be undone. It cannot be an ordinary backup: $backupClass
# writes <cls>, and <cls> is the very copy the restore is reading from — the
# backup would eat its own source. $copyClass is no use either, for the same
# reason: it takes its target name from the source and would collide.
#
# The name is _before and NOT _prev: _prev belongs to $holdBackup, and the next
# run deletes any _prev it finds in a vault. A net under that name would be
# swept away by the next script that touched the class.
#
# ONE _before per class. The next restore of the same class replaces it. A net
# for the last restore, not a history.
#
# The method count is compared but never used to refuse: this is a net, and a
# net that refuses to be spread is worse than one that is spread badly. The
# note says so and the caller can put it in the protocol.
# Returns a note WITHOUT a closing full stop, so a caller can place it.
If isclear(pClassRef)
	Quit method 'no live class, so no net was needed'
End If
If isclear(pVaultRef)
	Quit method 'no vault, so NO net was written'
End If
Calculate cName as con(pClassRef.$name,'_before')
If pVaultRef.$classes.$findname(cName)
	Do pVaultRef.$classes.$remove(pVaultRef.$classes.$findname(cName).$ref)
End If
Set reference newRef to pVaultRef.$classes.$add(pClassRef.$classtype,cName)
If isclear(newRef)
	Quit method con('NO net: ',cName,' could not be created')
End If
Do newRef.$classdata.$assign(pClassRef.$classdata) Returns ok
# never read through the add-returned reference (A8.6)
Set reference newRef to pVaultRef.$classes.$findname(cName)
If isclear(newRef)
	Quit method con('NO net: ',cName,' did not land')
End If
Calculate ok as newRef.$methods.$count=pClassRef.$methods.$count
# who writes, saves (persistence law)
Save class [con(pVaultRef.$name,'.',cName)]
Quit method con('net ',cName,pick(ok,' written, but its method count does NOT match the live class',' written'))